   "he": "בִּרְכַּת הַמָּזוֹן — דִּכְתִיב: ״וְאָכַלְתָּ וְשָׂבָעְתָּ וּבֵרַכְתָּ אֶת ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ״ — בְּכׇל לָשׁוֹן שֶׁאַתָּה מְבָרֵךְ.",
   "en": "§ It is stated in the mishna that «Grace after Meals» may be recited in any language. «As it is written: “And you shall eat, and be satisfied, and bless the Lord your God”» (Deuteronomy 8:10). The word “bless” is homiletically interpreted to mean: «In any language that you bless.»"
